From 7d2f939d3ae80bc8a70669a37389e2ea192e991f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: halt95 <halt95@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 04:08:13 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 01/58] worker: capture-safe guard-telemetry infrastructure,
 default off

Shared machinery for device-side bounds guards: persistent int64 counters per
site, written by guarded kernels and read by a background thread. The reader
starts only after warm-up and CUDA-graph capture and never waits on the
compute stream; a read failure arms the stop rather than popping the buffer.
Shutdown does one synchronous final drain so a hit on the last step is
reported before teardown. Release default: off.
---
